<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistani cotton market remained shut on Tuesday for a local religious holiday, the private Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) said.</p>
<p>Monday's official spot rates issued by the KCA in rupees per maund were:				  Monday	   Sunday</p>
<p>    NIAB-78				  2,542.50	 2,487.50</p>
<p>    K-68				     2,597.50	 2,570.00</p>
<p>    MNH-93				   2,618.50	 2,591.00</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 Pakistani rupees)</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
